Independent joint-posterior references

The small fixtures were defined during joint-sampler development and retain
fixed design matrices, responses and priors. They contain no fitted package
objects. The reference distributions integrate the statistical target, without
calling the production sampler or using its transition implementation.

exact-reference.R uses Gaussian raw-moment recurrences and analytic
inverse-gamma integration, followed by one-dimensional interaction quadrature.
quadrature-reference.R uses Gaussian/Gamma quadrature on the observed binary
or censored likelihood; fixtures retain both resolutions and their discrepancy.
availability-reference.R enumerates the available selection indicators and
integrates each platform's normalized MRF prior. BMS interactions are fixed zero.

To regenerate and compare, create an empty output directory and run:
  Rscript .github/reference/regenerate.R OUTPUT_DIRECTORY
The script never overwrites the checked-in fixtures. Refined observed-data
quadrature is intentionally separate from routine CI because of its cost.

verify-joint-reference.R runs four 30,000-draw chains per case and compares
posterior moments and model probabilities. Its quantile companion checks
marginal CDFs including exclusion point masses. Monte Carlo tolerance is stated
in the script; this is a stochastic numerical check, not a proof of convergence
for every possible dataset. Raw chains and discrepancy tables are CI artifacts.

native-bridge.R only converts fixture layouts to the registered native input
schema. It contains no sampling algorithm. Public data preparation, predictions,
interval summaries, CV splits and parallel equivalence are covered by the
installed test suite.
